{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CxQ1M3G4p5216VHqn5veEX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/01-016-what-is-graph-rag-how-does-it-differ-from-standard-rag.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** Knowledge graph (nodes = entities, edges = typed relationships) replaces or augments flat vector index\n- **Mechanism:** Two-phase — offline LLM-driven entity extraction + graph build (Neo4j, Kuzu, Leiden clustering); online entity-anchored traversal for local search, pre-built community summaries for global search\n- **Tradeoff table:** Standard RAG vs Graph RAG across setup cost, multi-hop quality, latency, and maintenance\n- **When NOT to use:** High-churn corpora (news) where graph construction cost and staleness outweigh benefits\n- **Pitfalls:** Calling it \"just RAG with a graph DB,\" over-recommending it universally, skipping the local vs global search distinction (Microsoft GraphRAG 2024)\n- **Cross-links:** Q12 (RAG pipeline), Q13 (embeddings), Q14 (chunking)\n\nNext up: **Q17 — What is reflection in the context of LLM agents?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":55836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3e2676c-ac32-4921-bd7b-985f4d002e27","uuid":"42356006-0663-4b78-93c2-09791c65350d"}
